<title>USA: Halsey withdraws ANDAs to get off FDA list.</title>
<headline>Halsey withdraws ANDAs to get off FDA list.</headline>
<dateline>BROOKLYN, N.Y. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Halsey Drug Co Inc said on Thursday it withrew four abbreviated new drug applications (ANDA) and halted sales of the affected products on October 23, in order to be taken off a U.S. FDA restricted list.</p>
<p>The company said it took the action in anticipation of its release from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration application integrity policy list and its restrictions.</p>
<p>Halsey Drug had been placed on this list in 1993, after an FDA investigation found inconsistencies in the company's record-keeping, a Halsey spokeswoman said.</p>
